sbc — Bluetooth low-complexity, subband codec (SBC) library
Vendored from https://github.com/nefarius/libsbc (fork of bluez sbc,
modified to build natively on Windows with MSVC).

Upstream: https://github.com/bluez/sbc  (git.kernel.org pub/scm/bluetooth/sbc.git)
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later  (see LICENSE.LGPL)

Used here to decode mSBC frames (HFP, 16kHz mono) from the AJAZZ voice mouse.
Only the decoder path (sbc_init_msbc / sbc_decode) is exercised at runtime.

Local decoder patches (2026-10-24), in sbc.c:
- Reject non-positive unpack results before initializing the synthesis state or
  committing decoded format/length metadata. A bad first sync word or reserved
  byte must not leave the decoder initialized with invalid filter offsets.
- Clear *written at entry, including argument errors and parse-only calls.
- Check consumed >= len * 8 before reading an audio bit, so truncated input
  cannot read one byte past its declared length.
The valid-frame synthesis path is unchanged. Real-library regressions in
src/msbc.rs and tests/golden.rs cover rejected frames followed by valid streams;
the checked-in golden PCM must remain byte-for-byte identical.
